#   Beagle-lite

This project implements beagle-lite functionality for git repos.

Build: quickjab is standalone — it carries dog/ (libdog) and test/ (the
jab-shared API suite) as submodules, no jab tree involved:

    cmake -S <quickjab> -B build -GNinja \
        -DJAB_JSRC=<this tree> -DQUICKJAB_JSRC_PACK=ON
    ninja -C build quickjab

Layout: `index/` reads the lane and the ODB, `view/` turns an arg into hunks
(one module per verb), `render/` turns hunks into bytes (`plain` `ansi` `html`
over `wrap` + `theme`), `door.js` turns a target into a view, and `main.js`
`pager.js` `http.js` `merge.js` `chat.js` are the apps.

Usage — a terminal with no flag pages coloured hunks; otherwise one mode flag
picks the sink, `--plain` (also what a pipe defaults to), `--color`, `--html`:

 -  `lite` — in a git repo: index it, open the `list` browser; elsewhere as `lite <path>`
 -  `lite <path>...` — page files/dirs off the filesystem
 -  `lite index [<repo>]` — build/refresh `<repo>/.git/be/`; lazy, fully derived
 -  `lite lindex [<target>]` — backlink suspects; lazy, tip blobs only
     1. bare: bring the LINK rows up to the tip
     2. `<target>`: the paths that may link to a file or a ticket code
 -  `lite log [<hex>|<path>]` — commit log, newest first; off-mainline rows grey
     1. bare: the checked-out tip's ancestry
     2. `<hex>`: that commit's ancestry
     3. `<path>`: the file's revisions
 -  `lite commit [<hex>]` — one commit, header + message; tree/parent hashes are links
 -  `lite diff [<hex>|<path>]` — the token-level diff
     1. bare: worktree vs HEAD
     2. `<hex>`: that commit vs its first parent
     3. `<path>`: that file/dir only
 -  `lite list [<path>][?<rev>]` — dir browser: marker, name, last commit, age
 -  `lite cat <path>[?<rev>]` — the file's own bytes, syntax-painted
 -  `lite tree [<hex>|<path>][?<rev>]` — raw git-tree rows, `..` row when descended
 -  `lite blob <hexlet>` — a blob by object name
 -  `lite http [--port <n>]` — the same views over HTTP on localhost:8034, read-only
     1. a `.md` URL renders as a page, links resolved; `.mkd` stays painted
    1. an `.rst` URL renders the reST subset; directives and tables show literal
     2. `/raw/<path>` is the painted source, and each view links to the other
     3. `/bytes/<path>[?<rev>]` ships the file's raw bytes; a rendered image points there
 -  `lite install [<repo>]` — register lite as the repo's git merge driver and pre-commit hook
 -  `lite hook [<repo>]` — the pre-commit pass: fresh `file:line(:col)` refs in the staged text become `file:OFF:HASHLET` permalinks, re-staged
 -  `lite merge <base> <ours> <theirs> [-o <out>] [-p <path>]` — CRDT 3-way file merge
     1. clean: merged bytes over `<ours>` (or `<out>`), exit 0
     2. conflict: markerless weave, exit 1
     3. binary/oversize: falls back to `git merge-file`
 -  `lite chat [dir] [outdir]` — Claude session logs to StrictMark pages, append-only reruns

